1
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,140
奥列格 第二桌的客人
Oleg, the people at table two

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,480
想知道他们的蔬菜汉堡里有什么
want to know what's in the veggie burger.

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:06,940
不 他们不会想知道的
No. They don't.

4
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:12,780
好吧 无所谓
Eh. That's fine.

5
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:13,720
他们还想要再添
They wanted refills,

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,440
所以我估计也不会再过去了
so I'm probably not gonna go back there anyway.

7
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,500
麦克斯上哪去了
Where's Max?

8
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,140
这菜在这边放了这么久
This plate has been here so long,

9
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,700
里面的三文鱼都要变成沙门氏菌[音似]了
the salmon is turning into Salmonella.

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,660
她跟新来的洗碗工去"休息"一下了
She took a break with the new dishwasher.

11
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:29,680
麦克斯 我还以为你从后面溜出去了
Max, I thought you slipped out the back.

12
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:32,400
他的确"溜出来"了一会 但我又帮他塞回去了
He did for a minute, but I popped him back in.

13
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:40,760
新闻快讯 跟你的同事上床
This just in, work is so much more fun

14
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:41,920
会让工作变得欢乐无边
when you're sleeping with a co-worker.

15
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:44,800
麦克斯 刚才的确很爽
Max, that was good.

16
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:46,675
喊五次额滴神啊的爽度
It was five Hail Marys good.

17
00:00:46,675 --> 00:00:50,687
我们让这些脏盘子变更"脏"了
I think we made these dishes dirtier.

18
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,560
麦克斯 他的确很萌
Max, he's cute,

19
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,140
但听到他这口音你怎么还硬得起来
but how can you even stay hard with that accent?

20
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:01,580
"狗来 麦克苏 让偶跟里爱爱一下下"
"Come here, Max. I wanna hump ya a wee bit".

21
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:06,200
我能说啥 我一直对
What can I say, I always had a thing

22
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,860
幸运符麦片盒上的小人情有独钟(爱尔兰妖精)
for the guy on the box of Lucky Charms.

23
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:23,920
大家安安
Hey, everybody.

24
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:30,180
看 我买了个健美计步器
Look, I got me a Fitbit.

25
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:37,116
只要再走二十万步
Only 200,000 more steps

26
00:01:37,116 --> 00:01:40,634
婚礼上就能身材"健美" "步步"生莲了
before I get a bit more fit for my wedding.

27
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:42,320
很厉害了
That's impressive.

28
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,500
我连十二步都走不完呢
I couldn't even make it through 12 steps.

29
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,580
麦克斯
Hey, Max.

30
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,460
我的伴娘你还好吗
How's my maid of honor?

31
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,020
卡洛琳
Hey, Caroline.

32
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,420
我平凡无奇的婚礼宾客你还好吗
How's my run-of-the-mill wedding guest?

33
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,740
我很好 这话说得有说服力吗
I'm doing great. Did that sound convincing?

34
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,460
我每天早上都花一小时在浴室里
'Cause I've been practicing it in the bathroom mirror

35
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:02,740
对着镜子练习回答这问题
for an hour every morning.

36
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:05,340
我看过 以后你在练习时
I know, I've got to stop sitting on the toilet

37
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,140
我就不进去蹲坑了
while you do that.

38
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:10,600
麦克斯 来谈谈伴娘礼服
Max, let's talk bridesmaid dresses.

39
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:12,220
我无所谓 你给我啥我都穿
I don't care, I'll wear anything.

40
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:15,140
我穿灰狗大巴司机制服去参加高中舞会呢
I wore a Greyhound Bus driver's uniform to my prom.

41
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:17,740
我当时刚下班就直接去了
I was coming straight from work.

42
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,780
我已经决定要穿
Well, I have decided to wear

43
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,800
科臣斯基奶奶当年的婚纱
Grandma Kuchenski's wedding gown.

44
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:27,040
对啊 我家族里所有的女人都穿
Yeah, all of the women in my family wore it.

45
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:29,433
除了我丝薇提与蕾提阿姨
Everyone except aunts Svetti and Letti,

46
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:32,460
那是因为她们是腹部连着的连体婴
'cause, well, they're attached at the abdomen.

47
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,360
她来了
There she is.

48
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,940
我墨西哥大香肠蛋饼必备的火辣辣酱
The hot sauce for my Huevos Mancheros.

49
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,380
苏菲宝贝 我弄到你想要的那个了
Hey, Sophie, baby, I got you what you want.

50
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,540
奥列格 没人想要肝炎好吗
Oleg, no one wants hepatitis.

51
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,240
正式定下了
It's official.

52
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,680
我们的婚礼会出现在《时报》上
Our wedding's gonna be in The Times.

53
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,260
奥列格 你凭什么能上《时报》
Oleg, how are you gonna be in The Times?

54
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,820
人家《时报》很挑剔的哇
The Times tends to be picky

55
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,980
而你是属于"很挑剔的挖"鼻屎
and you tend to be more "picky your nose."

56
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:06,960
我的第二次婚礼就上《时报》呢
You know, my second wedding made The Times.

57
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:10,160
因为我的第一任妻子跑来往我脚开了一枪
'Cause my first wife showed up and shot me in the leg.

58
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,380
是薇兰卡 我妹
That's Vlanka, my sister.

59
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,580
她是我另一个伴娘
She's my other bridesmaid.

60
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:22,940
其实我跟她不太亲 不过我可怜她
Yeah, we're not that close, but I feel bad for her

61
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,700
因为她是那种都成年了还长雀斑的人
'cause she's one of those adults with freckles.

62
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:31,840
麦克斯 你会上《时报》呢
Max, you're going to be in The Times!

63
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:35,940
上《时报》 然后穿着苏菲挑的鬼东西
In The Times, wearing God knows what Sophie will pick.

64
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:40,240
她可是有一抽屉"健身时戴的王冠"的那种人
I mean, she has a drawer full of diamond tiaras for the gym.

65
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,440
您好 请问姐两位在聊啥呢
Hello, what are you two talking about?

66
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:47,220
在讨论要故意忽视哪桌客人吗
Deciding which tables to ignore?

67
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:50,120
我们在讨论苏菲的品味
We're talking about Sophie's taste.

68
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,280
我去 小婊砸们
Oh, bitch, please.

69
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:54,880
别闹了
Come on.

70
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:58,040
我早餐纤维棒都比她的品味来得"好味"
My morning fiber cookie has better taste than Sophie.

71
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,760
姑娘们 薇兰卡滚蛋了
Girls, Vlanka's out.

72
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:05,360
雀斑妹就算了 还有胆跟老娘叫板
She has an attitude and freckles.

73
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,900
对啊 这也太超过了
Yeah. I mean, that's too far.

74
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:12,740
所以 恭喜你啦 卡洛琳
So, Caroline, congratulations!

75
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,960
你就是我新的伴娘啦
You're my new bridesmaid!

76
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,220
我找到我喜欢的伴娘礼服了
Okay, I found a bridesmaid's dress that I like.

77
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,700
但我们买得起的唯一办法是
But the only way we can afford it is

78
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,060
把你卖给分类广告网上那个亚美尼亚人
if I sell you to that Armenian guy on Craigslist.

79
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:30,800
屁咧
No way.

80
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,020
他们爱吃的鹰嘴豆泥 我吃几口就想吐
I get sick of hummus after four bites.

81
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:36,160
麦克斯 这件事我们得占据主导权
Max, we have to take charge of this.

82
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:38,060
因为无论苏菲给我们挑了什么婚纱
Because whatever bridesmaid's dress Sophie picks

83
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:39,580
都会像泰勒·派瑞导的电影一样
is like a Tyler Perry movie.

84
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,280
我看都不用看就知道难看到死
I don't have to see it to know it's gonna be awful.

85
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:48,280
我们就自己找件高雅漂亮的
We'll find something classy, and beautiful,

86
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,000
然后强行逼她接受[硬塞进她喉咙]
and just shove it down her throat.

87
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,660
谁要把什么东西塞进谁的喉咙啊
Who's shoving what down whom?

88
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:57,000
如果这个你们没有故事说 我有
And if you don't have a story, I do.

89
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:03,040
强哥 我和麦克斯被人情绑架去当伴娘
John, Max and I got roped into being bridesmaids.

90
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:03,980
别说了
Stop.

91
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,260
你刚才的"绑"字让我两眼放光
You had me at rope.

92
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,060
但"伴娘"两个字让我兴趣全无
You lost me at bridesmaids.

93
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:10,240
我会在迎宾员那里站着 看看礼服
I'll be at the hostess stand, looking at dresses

94
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,180
然后默默地祈祷有颗小行星
and silently wishing for an asteroid

95
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,440
撞上地球 灭了全世界
to wipe us off the planet.

96
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:16,280
如果祈祷这玩意有效 那现在地球上
If wishes made things happen, we'd been in the middle

97
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,120
应该早就被行尸给毁灭世界了
of a zombie apocalypse right now.

98
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,600
姑娘们
Hey, girls.

99
00:05:22,020 --> 00:05:23,740
我刚收到从波兰寄来的婚纱了
My dress just arrived from Poland

100
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,880
我等不及要给你们俩看了
and I'm bustin' for you to see it.

101
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:28,720
一边看 一边吃着你们14块钱一个的布丁
See it while I eat one of your $14 puddings.

102
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,500
苏菲 我有在研究礼服颜色
Sophie, I've been looking at color choices,

103
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,480
你觉得我们两个穿肉色[裸身]如何
and how would you feel about us in a nude?

104
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:37,000
麦克斯有本钱能裸身
Max could go nude but

105
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,540
但你胸口余额不足 裸身就算了吧
you don't have the rack to pull it off.

106
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:42,540
有人有刀吗
Does anyone have a knife?

107
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,660
麦克斯 为什么你在甜品吧工作
Max, why do you have a switchblade

108
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:49,980
身上却会带着弹簧刀啊
to work in a dessert bar?

109
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,340
我妈从小叮咛我出门要带"保护措施"
My mother always told me to carry protection.

110
00:05:54,994 --> 00:05:58,295
屏息以待科臣斯基奶奶的婚纱吧
Wait 'til you see Grandma Kuchenski's dress.

111
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,480
因为强逼吉普赛人当劳工是非法的了
You know, forced gypsy labor is illegal now.

112
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:06,140
来看看
Here we go.

113
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:15,780
苏菲 你奶奶是千年老妖吗
Sophie, was your grandma the Crypt Keeper?

114
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,680
外面这是怎么回事
What's going on out here?

115
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,920
空气中这些白色粉末是啥玩意
What's all that white powder in the air?

116
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:26,040
我是想开餐厅 不是80年代吸白粉的舞厅
I'm trying to run a restaurant, not an 80's disco.

117
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:29,160
闭上你的鸟嘴
Oh, put a sock in it.

118
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:32,280
我可是买了你抢钱布丁的贵客
I'm buying one of your freaking overpriced puddings.

119
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:39,260
我本来要发火的 可现在又有点被你吸引
I'd get mad but I'm mildly attracted to you right now.

120
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:42,940
只是有点而已吗
Just mildly?

121
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,780
现在我倒是要发火了
I mean, now I'm getting mad.

122
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,740
抱歉 婚礼的烦心事
Sorry. Wedding drama.

123
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,720
她的婚纱突然就灰飞烟灭了
Her dress just fell completely to pieces...

124
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:52,880
就像我预测中自己不久后的将来
like I'm assuming I'll do in the near future.

125
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,800
婚礼需要任何东西
Whatever you need bridal,

126
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:57,580
就去布鲁克林区的罗森福家买
go to Rosenfeld's in Brooklyn.

127
00:06:58,020 --> 00:07:00,480
在我又穷又直的那会 我去那里买的婚纱
That's where I got my dress when I was broke and straight.

128
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:04,440
原来你不是一直都是拉拉啊
So you weren't always into women?

129
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,000
我一直都是拉拉啊
Of course I was.

130
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,920
除了加入邪教的那三年
Except those three years in Scientology.

131
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,800
看来我们三个
Well, it looks like the three of us

132
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,680
得去逛一下婚纱和礼服了
are going to go dress shopping now.

133
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,920
是啊 不过我得先去洗一下手
Yeah. And you know, I got to go wash my hands

134
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:23,020
我现在手上沾满了老女人的DNA
'cause they're covered in old lady DNA.

135
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,540
看来是得去一趟了
Well, that's that.

136
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:30,580
跟苏菲去逛街就跟当年
Shopping with Sophie is like when I worked

137
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:32,060
我在泰式按摩院工作时一样
in a Thai massage parlor.

138
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,240
都得"下去"
We are going down.

139
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:41,800
但如果我们早苏菲一步去
Not if we go before Sophie

140
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:45,020
把她会喜欢的难看伴娘裙全藏起来就没事了
and hide every ugly bridesmaid's dress that Sophie would like.

141
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:47,580
如果她看不到 就不能逼我们穿啦
If she can't see them, she can't make us wear them.

142
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,940
你怎么这么快就能想出这招
How did you come up with that so fast?

143
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:51,820
我在2010年时就用过这招了
It's the same plan I used in 2010

144
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:53,600
那年我给克林顿总统女儿当伴娘
when I was a bridesmaid for Chelsea Clinton.

145
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:56,780
伴娘服难看 她的色鬼老爸还跟踪我进衣帽间
Bad dress and then her father followed me into the coat room.

146
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:04,280
看看这地方
Look at this place.

147
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:05,940
让我想起那部电影
It reminds me of that movie.

148
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:08,180
-《伴娘》吗 -不 是《猛鬼街》
- Bridesmaids? - No, Nightmare on Elm Street.

149
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,820
卡洛琳 我不知道你有什么好担心的
I don't know what you're worried about, Caroline.

150
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:13,920
我觉得它们都挺漂漂啊
I think they're all quite lovely.

151
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,400
纳西 别说了
Nash, please.

152
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,360
你就是个从爱尔兰来的穷人
You're a poor person from Ireland.

153
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:21,640
如果我是想知道哪里免费腿部支架之类的
I'll ask your opinion when I need to know where to go

154
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,940
我会问你
to get free leg braces.

155
00:08:24,335 --> 00:08:26,109
麦克斯 你还真没说错
You were right, Max.

156
00:08:26,109 --> 00:08:30,100
她有时候真的就是个"B"
She can be a real "B" sometimes.

157
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:32,559
对不起啦 但我真不知道为什么带他来
I'm sorry, but I don't even know why he's here.

158
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:35,665
上你·没商量先生来这
Bonin' O'Brien here...

159
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:40,820
用美色帮我们引开那些女销售员
is gonna distract the sales lady

160
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,400
然后我们就能藏起那些难看礼服
while we hide the ugly dresses.

161
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,600
您好 女士们
Hello, ladies.

162
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,060
计划不变
Same plan.

163
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:49,360
谁是那位幸运的新娘啊
