00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:25,980
现在想想 那"玩意"也让我"作呕"
Come to think of it, that made me gag, too.

338
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:29,200
好了 结束了
Okay. Done.

339
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:35,080
你听 有人在试衣间里哭
listen, crying in a women's dressing room?

340
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:38,420
不管你是谁 妹子 现在流行大屁股
Whoever it is, girl, big butts are in.

341
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:44,180
那是苏菲的哭声
That's Sophie's cry.

342
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:46,260
我知道 我曾在通风孔听过她的哭声
I know, 'cause I hear it through the vent

343
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,540
当时她在看电视剧《音乐之乡》
when she watches Nashville.

344
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:50,940
苏菲
Sophie?

345
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:53,860
不是
No.

346
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,540
你没事吧
Are you okay?

347
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:01,040
不是我 但我没事
It's not me, but I'm okay.

348
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:08,040
苏菲 你为什么哭
Sophie, why are you crying?

349
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:11,720
当我听到你抱怨裙子的话时...
When I heard what you said about the dresses...

350
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,580
让我...
It's just--

351
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,740
感觉就像 有点像
It's almost, kind of like,

352
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,920
你觉得我的品味差之类的
you think I have bad taste or something.

353
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,320
没有
No.

354
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,600
卡洛琳觉得你的品味很棒
Caroline thinks you have great taste.

355
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,160
真的吗
She does?

356
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:37,060
那她说出来啊
Well, then she should say so.

357
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:38,780
现在就说
Now.

358
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:47,120
苏菲 我觉得你拥有独一无二的个人风格
Well, Sophie, I think you have your own unique style.

359
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:50,300
而我觉得...
And I think...

360
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:54,840
我没听见"很棒"或"品味"两个词
that I didn't hear the words "great" or "taste."

361
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:57,940
苏菲 你干嘛在乎我怎么想
Sophie, what do you even care what I think?

362
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:58,880
快说
Just say it!

363
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:03,420
苏菲 我觉得你的品味很棒
Sophie, I think you have great taste.

364
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:06,500
真的吗
You do?

365
00:19:11,716 --> 00:19:15,320
那我们还在坐着干嘛
Then, what are we doing sitting here?

366
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:18,320
快去把那两条裙子抢回来
Let's go and get those dresses back!

367
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:20,440
快 帮我一下
Come on. Help me!

368
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:27,320
那俩妞已经把裙子买走了
Those other girls already took them.

369
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:29,440
什么
What?

370
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,740
至少我们不必穿着在婚礼上
Well, at least we don't have to wear those ugly,

371
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:39,460
穿着那条难看的黄色伴娘裙了
yellow bridesmaid dresses at the wedding.

372
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:41,760
是啊 现在你们只需在这穿着
Yup. Now, you only have to wear

373
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:43,700
这条难看的黄色制服裙 每晚都穿
ugly, yellow dresses here, every night.

374
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:46,540
这是发生在我身上最棒的事情了
This is the best thing that's happened to me

375
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:48,460
上次还是我发现我手臂上奇怪的痣
since I realized that weird mole on my arm was

376
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:51,380
只是一颗早餐麦片 不是癌症
just a Grape-Nut and not cancer.

377
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,760
姑娘们 好消息
Girls, great news.

378
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,420
你把阿憨塞进微波炉
You stuffed Han in the microwave

379
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:55,440
准备按下电源键吗
and you're ready to hit power?

380
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:57,740
拜托 我们早试过了
Come on. We've tried.

381
00:19:57,860 --> 00:19:58,920
你知道他塞不进去
You know he doesn't fit.

382
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,680
唯一一样他太大进不去的东西
The one thing he's too big for.

383
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:05,640
我请伊利亚·乔比奇当我们的婚礼摄影师
No, I got Ilia Jorbich to be our wedding photographer.

384
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:08,560
他是《华沙时报》最厉害的摄影师
He's the best photographer at The Warsaw Times.

385
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:11,500
他也是唯一双臂还没被炸掉的摄影师
Well, he's the only one who still has both arms.

386
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:15,140
等等 所以是《华沙时报》
Wait, it's the Warsaw Times?

387
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:18,740
一直以来 我都以为是《纽约时报》
All this time, I've been thinking it was The New York Times.

388
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,220
《纽约时报》
New York Times?

389
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:21,960
这比它独家多了
This is much more exclusive.

390
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:23,600
你只能在两种地方买到
You can only get it in two places.

391
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,560
波兰和新泽西一家有卖导弹的熟食店
Poland and the deli in New Jersey that sells missiles.

392
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,320
这太棒了
This is amazing.

393
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:32,460
我在《纽约时报》的华丽回归的机会还在
My comeback in The New York Times has been preserved.

394
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,900
麦克斯 我要好好笑一个
Max, I'm gonna go ahead and smile.

395
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:36,240
我的生活又变美好了
My life is good again.

396
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:38,820
先别笑 苏菲告诉我
Don't smile yet, 'cause Sophie told me

397
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:40,940
因为你说她品味好
that because you said she had such good taste,

398
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:43,260
她要亲自设计我们的礼服
she's designing our dresses herself.

399
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:45,200
美梦一秒钟就破功了吗
What was that, like a second?

400
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,860
是啊 你刚直接从最美好的时光
Yup. You just went from the best of times

401
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:50,000
掉到了《华沙时光[报]》
to The Warsaw Times.
